@startuml implementation-issue-states
' cumin-works - the states of an implementation issue, with the action names only.
' Each category page holds the guards and what cumin does
' (implementation, checks, review, merge).
' A state is a label on GitHub, written without "cumin/status/".
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "ready" as Ready
state "implementing" as Implementing
state "checking" as Checking
state "reviewing" as Reviewing
state "awaiting-merge-decision" as MergeDecision
state "awaiting-base" as AwaitingBase
state "merging" as Merging
state "awaiting-decision" as Decision

[*] --> Ready : a Maintainer adds ready
Ready --> Implementing : request the implementation
Implementing --> Implementing : request the implementation again
Implementing --> Checking : wait for the checks
Implementing --> Decision : stop the implementation
Checking --> Implementing : request a check fix,\nrequest a conflict resolution
Checking --> Decision : stop for failed checks,\nstop for missing checks
Checking --> Reviewing : request the review
Reviewing --> Reviewing : request the review again,\nrequest the cause
Reviewing --> Implementing : request a review fix
Reviewing --> Checking : go back to the checks
Reviewing --> Decision : stop the review,\nstop at the round limit
Reviewing --> Merging : start the merge (risk low)
Reviewing --> MergeDecision : ask for the merge decision (risk medium, high)
Reviewing --> AwaitingBase : wait for the base
MergeDecision --> Merging : start the merge
MergeDecision --> Implementing : request an assignee review fix,\nrequest a conflict resolution
AwaitingBase --> Implementing : update onto the default branch
AwaitingBase --> Decision : stop the implementation
Merging --> Merging : merge
Merging --> Checking : go back to the checks
Merging --> Implementing : request a conflict resolution
Merging --> Decision : stop the merge
Merging --> [*] : close the merged issue
Decision --> Ready : the Assignee answers and adds ready

@enduml
